# Security & Privacy (RAOS Ch.20)

Full doc: `docs/raos/chapter-20-security-privacy.md`.

## Principles

- Privacy by Design; users own Trip, Workspace, Conversation, Memory, DNA.
- Classify data: Public / Internal / Private / Sensitive; protect accordingly.
- Memory/DNA/Learning require explicit consent; not default-all-on.
- Users can view/export/delete; support Forget Everything.
- Workspace private by default; sharing is opt-in.
- Sharing a Trip must not leak Memory/DNA/Conversation unless separately authorized.
- Collaboration may edit Trip only — never creator Memory/DNA/Learning/preferences.
- Learning may be disabled; then stop Memory/DNA/learning updates.
- Explain Memory/DNA-influenced recommendations when asked/used.
- Encrypt Private/Sensitive in transit and at rest; API authz by identity + membership + permission.
- Audit sensitive ops (delete memory, share workspace/trip, permission changes).
- New feature checklist: personal data? consent? deletable? viewable? If no → redesign before ship.
